{#- The home backdrop. ORDER IS DEPTH:
      orb        furthest back
      hill 3, 2  far and middle hills
      torii      in front of those, behind the near hill
      hill 1     nearest, painting over the gate's feet
    The hills share one viewBox and are placed by the `.hill` rule in main.css;
    the orb and gate are boxes placed on their own (hence no `hill` class).

    With orbToggles set (index.njk) the orb is the theme switch: it ships
    disabled + aria-hidden and theme.js enables it, so without JS it is just a
    drawing. aria-hidden is on each decorative child, not the wrapper, because
    a focusable element inside an aria-hidden subtree still takes a tab stop.
    Reusable elsewhere by dropping lines; without orbToggles the orb is only
    decoration. #}
<div class="hills">
  {%- if orbToggles %}
  <button class="orb" type="button" data-theme-toggle disabled aria-hidden="true"></button>
  {%- else %}
  <span class="orb" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  {%- endif %}
  <span class="hill hill-3" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="hill hill-2" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="torii" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="hill hill-1" aria-hidden="true"></span>
</div>
